Package: Reservoir
Type: Package
Title: Modular Stochastic Epidemic Simulation and Synthetic Surveillance Data Generation
Version: 0.3.2
Authors@R: person("Reiden-Magdaleno", email = "reiden@umich.edu",
                  role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A modular pipeline for generating labeled synthetic epidemic
    trajectories across human-to-human, vector-borne, and environmental
    transmission mechanisms. Model structure is declared explicitly through
    a compartment/edge specification, allowing SIR, SEIR, SIS, SEIS, SIAR,
    SEIAR and related skeletons to be generated from a common set of
    adaptive tau-leaping C++ engines. Combines a hierarchical parameter
    sampler, next-generation-matrix Rt computation, scheduled and reactive
    (threshold-triggered) intervention policies, and a multi-stage
    observation model that adds realistic surveillance noise
    (under-reporting, weekday effects, reporting delays, laboratory batch
    noise, and overdispersion).
